      "message": "[warning] Line 3897: 🟡 `packFetched_` is cleared via `exchange(false)` before the merge attempt, so a transient failure in `repack(path, MAX_PACKS)` (I/O error, temporary libgit2 failure, etc.) drops the retry signal until another fetch receives objects. This can leave repositories above the pack limit indefinitely. Keep the flag set on failed/aborted repack (e.g., set it back to `true` when merge fails, or only clear after a successful/no-op determination) so cleanup is retried.",
